 "text": "Hi, how you doing right now? They' looking for dark, quiet spots under sinks and drawers. A bright tent completely covers one, and a mesh roof keeps it open. Stick a few sticks in the holes, or a small piece of clothing worn only inside, and watch for everyone to flick their wings. Calmly sprays with insect spray, then leave the tent closed. Keep the tent on future trips, the wasps don't recognize the spot after few weeks.",
